    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) computed on creation, per the spec.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response schema with `membershipLevel` (integer, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`), so the generated `OwnerDto` now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived `@Transient getMembershipLevel()`: starts at 1, adds 1 when an email is present, adds 1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3. It recomputes from persisted fields (`email`, `namesakeCount`), so it survives a DB round-trip (the test creates then re-reads via `GET`). Level 4 is left unimplemented as noted (reserved for tenure).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Removed the old `membershipTier` expression mapping; MapStruct now auto-maps `membershipLevel` from `owner.getMembershipLevel()` by name.\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Updated the create audit line to record `membershipLevel={}` instead of the (former) tier, evaluated after `namesakeCount` is set so the level is accurate.\n\n**Design note:** The old tier folded in `householdSize` (GOLD tier); the new level spec deliberately does not \u2014 it uses only email presence and `namesakeCount`, with 4 reserved for tenure. This intentionally changes the prior tier behaviour, as the spec calls out.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` test (unique owner + email \u2192 `membershipLevel == 3`) passes, and the audit log confirms `membershipLevel=3` is recorded.",
